{
 "title": "Absorbing boundary: CPML on a matched microstrip",
 "text": [
  "19 mm microstrip on L1 of the 4-layer stack (0.35 mm over 0.2 mm FR-4), 50 \u03a9 lumped ports. Whatever S11 the boundary adds shows as a reflection floor. kisi-fdtd's CPML (8 cells outside the domain, polynomial grading m = 3, CFS \u03b1) gives the same S11 with 16 cells, so it is converged; openEMS' PML_8 on the same mesh reflects about 8\u201314 dB more above 10 GHz. S21 agrees within 0.01 dB."
